      question: 'What is the difference between Jinas (paronomasia) and Tibaq (antithesis)?',
      answer: 'Both are figures from Ilm al-Badi. Jinas (paronomasia) is the use of two words that are similar or identical in sound but different in meaning. Types: (1) Jinas tam (perfect) — identical in letters, vowels, and number but different in meaning: هَلْ أَتَاكَ حَدِيثُ المُوسَى... وَالمُوسَى (the news of Musa/the razor — same letters, different meaning). (2) Jinas ghayr tam (imperfect) — similar but not identical. Tibaq (antithesis) is pairing two opposites in one expression to create contrast and impact. Types: (1) Tibaq ijab (affirmative antithesis): يَضْحَكُونَ... وَيَبْكُونَ (they laugh... and they weep — Quran 53:60); (2) Tibaq salab (negative antithesis): لَا تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلَا نَوْمٌ (neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him — Quran 2:255, Ayat al-Kursi).',
