      answer: 'Afʿal al-Tafdil expresses that something is superior in a quality or is the superlative of a quality. Pattern: أَفْعَل (masculine) / فُعْلَى (feminine). Formation from Form I adjectives: كَبِيرٌ → أَكْبَرُ (larger/largest); صَغِيرٌ → أَصْغَرُ (smaller/smallest); عَظِيمٌ → أَعْظَمُ (greater/greatest); كَثِيرٌ → أَكْثَرُ (more/most); قَلِيلٌ → أَقَلُّ (less/least). Conditions: (1) the adjective must be Form I; (2) it must be from a tri-literal root; (3) the quality must be gradable; (4) the root must not naturally be on the pattern afʿal (colors cannot form afʿal al-tafdil directly — أَحْمَرُ is a color adjective, not a comparative). The feminine form فُعْلَى: كُبْرَى، صُغْرَى، عُظْمَى، كُثْرَى. Usage in Quran: الله أَكْبَرُ (Allah is greater/greatest), وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن (and who is more unjust than...).',
