      answer: 'Surah al-Fatihah is called Umm al-Quran (أُمُّ القُرْآن) because it encompasses the central themes of the entire Quran: (1) Tawhid al-Rububiyyah — divine lordship: الحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ العَالَمِين; (2) Tawhid al-Uluhiyyah — exclusive worship: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ; (3) Tawhid al-Asma wal-Sifat — divine names and attributes: الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيم; (4) The Day of Judgment: مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّين; (5) Guidance — the ultimate human need: اهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ المُسْتَقِيم; (6) The distinction of paths. The Prophet ﷺ said: "There has not been revealed in the Torah, the Injeel, the Zabur, nor in the Quran a surah like it." (Tirmidhi — Hasan Sahih)',
