      question: 'What is the Ijaz al-Qurani (الإِعْجَاز القُرْآنِي — the inimitability of the Quran) and what are its dimensions?',
      answer: 'Al-Ijaz al-Qurani is the miraculous nature of the Quran — the quality by which it surpasses all human capacity to produce its like. Dimensions of ijaz: (1) Al-Ijaz al-Balaghi (linguistic/rhetorical inimitability) — the Quran\'s unmatched eloquence, composition, and rhetorical perfection; it challenged the Arabs — the greatest orators in history — and they could not produce its like (Quran 2:23, 10:38, 11:13, 17:88). (2) Al-Ijaz al-Ilmi (scientific inimitability) — references to natural phenomena that were not known at the time of revelation. (3) Al-Ijaz al-Ghaybi (unseen knowledge inimitability) — precise prophesies that were fulfilled. (4) Al-Ijaz al-Tashrii (legislative inimitability) — the perfection of its legal system. (5) Al-Ijaz al-Adadi (numerical inimitability) — some scholars discuss numerical patterns, though this is less established. Al-Jurjani\'s Dala\'il al-Ijaz focused on the rhetorical dimension as the primary and most verifiable form.',
