      answer: 'Al-Burhan fi Ulum al-Quran (The Proof in the Sciences of the Quran) by Badr al-Din Muhammad al-Zarkashi (d. 794 AH) is the most comprehensive classical work in ulum al-Quran (Quranic sciences). It covers 47 different sciences of the Quran in two volumes. Key topics: (1) The different modes of revelation and its forms; (2) Al-Makki wal-Madani; (3) Asbab al-Nuzul; (4) Al-Nasikh wal-Mansukh; (5) The ijaz of the Quran; (6) The sciences of qiraat; (7) The sciences of tafseer and its conditions; (8) Rhetorical sciences (balagha) in the Quran; (9) The tartib (ordering) of the Quran; (10) The asma (names) of the Quran. Al-Zarkashi\'s work was later abridged and expanded by al-Suyuti in Al-Itqan fi Ulum al-Quran — which became the standard reference text. Together, these two works constitute the comprehensive encyclopedia of Quranic sciences.',
